# Gate step 1199-aw6m — data, not code.
#
# Binds the host-scoped-criteria annotation. Drives the REAL selector over a
# SCRATCH ledger (hermetic since 1420-9jdf): the scratch tree symlinks the real
# scripts/, and its host-scoped row carries 1132-r4mt's criterion verbatim, so
# the subject is still whether the selector reads criteria real rows carry. The
# live-ledger version exited 3 whenever today's batch had no host-scoped row,
# which read as refused in every host's preflight on a clean tree.
#
# THE ARMS THAT MATTER ARE THE CONTROLS. Arm 2 re-runs as EACH host the criteria
# DO name and requires the mark to DISAPPEAR: without it a selector that marked
# every row would pass, which is noise and trains readers to ignore the line.
# Arm 3 requires the marked row to still be OFFERED — marking must never filter,
# because a host that cannot CLOSE a row can still reproduce, measure or split it.
# Arm 4 requires the rows naming no host to stay unmarked. Arm 5 requires the host
# vocabulary to come from the roster rather than a literal list that would drift.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking an offer carries the host constraint its row already states (1199-aw6m)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-selector-flags-host-scoped-criteria.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the selector's host-scoped annotation regressed (1199-aw6m) — either a row whose exit criteria name other hosts is being offered unmarked (so hosts keep claiming and releasing work they cannot close, as lenovinha did with 1132-r4mt), or the mark has widened into a blanket annotation, or worse it has begun WITHHOLDING rows; see the failing arm above"
STEP_OK="selector host-scoped criteria annotation check passed"
# Exit 3 now means only that no runnable plan binary resolved (or mktemp failed):
# the ledger is the fixture's own, so a batch with no host-scoped row cannot occur.
STEP_SKIP_EXIT=3
STEP_SKIP_DESC="no runnable tillandsias-plan resolved, so the selector could not be driven"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="tlatoanis-macbook-air 2026-09-26 darwin ok:host-scoped-criteria:6"
